e down temperatures  can be impacted water temperatures in  certain areas are impacted by damming so  there is a big movement and I have to  tell you I am sympathetic to this  movement that says you know hydro is not  really renewable and I think that  there's a sort of different way to think  about this it is we can call it  renewable in the sense that it is not  using up a resource the water flows  through and provides energy and then the  water still exists you're not burning up  the water and the way that we are when  we are when we're talking about oil or  coal but it is not sustainable and I  think that's really what makes it for me  a sustainable energy source is one that  is number one renewable but also has  environmental consequences that are not  destructive and in that sense I am  completely on board in saying wait a  second I am all about Costa Rica being  100% on renewable energy but 80% of that  renewable energy is hydro and hydro is  damaging to our planet what do you think  about this you can discuss this with us  on Facebook facebook.com slash David  Pakman show you can also discuss this  with us on reddit at david pakman.com  slash Reddit and of course I'm always  paying attention to my Twitter feed you  can reach me on Twitter at Dee Pakman
 

